title: MunnaBhai_Day1
tags: 
position: -7,-175
---

<<PlayBackgroundMusic Light_3>>
<<SetBGSprite MunnaTyreShop>>

// Scene Setup - Day 1 at the tire shop during busy afternoon
After noticing the long line of bicycles outside Munna Bhai's shop, Raju decides to visit during the busy afternoon to see if the skilled repairman needs help.

The tire shop buzzes with activity. Air pumps hiss and tire irons clang as Munna Bhai works through a mountain of repairs. Sweat beads on his forehead despite his practiced efficiency.

<<SetCharacterExpression "MunnaBhai" "Tired">>
MunnaBhai: Arre beta, you picked quite a day to visit!

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Quizzical">>
Raju: It looks very busy, bhai. Is everything alright?

<<SetCharacterExpression "MunnaBhai" "Worried">>
MunnaBhai: Everyone's bicycle needs repair at the same time, and I'm just one person with two hands.

<<SetCharacterExpression "MunnaBhai" "Pained">>
MunnaBhai: Look at this line - it's going to take me until midnight to fix all these punctures.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Excited">>
Raju: Munna bhai, you look exhausted! I have some free time. Can I help somehow?

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Smiling">>
Raju: I'd love to learn about bicycle repair work too.

<<SetCharacterExpression "MunnaBhai" "Skeptical">>
MunnaBhai: Help? Beta, this isn't child's play.

<<SetCharacterExpression "MunnaBhai" "Worried">>
MunnaBhai: These tires cost people their daily wages. One mistake means a customer's bicycle fails on the road.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Serious">>
Raju: I understand it's serious work, bhai. But I'm careful with tools and I learn quickly.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Confident">>
Raju: Maybe I could start with something simple? Just to help reduce your workload a little?

<<SetCharacterExpression "MunnaBhai" "Skeptical">>
MunnaBhai: Simple? There's nothing simple about keeping people's transportation working!

<<SetCharacterExpression "MunnaBhai" "Serious">>
MunnaBhai: Every tire must hold perfect pressure. Every patch must seal completely.

<<SetCharacterExpression "MunnaBhai" "Anxious">>
MunnaBhai: One failed repair and people can't get to work, school, or market.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Determined">>
Raju: That's exactly why I want to help, bhai!

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Proud">>
Raju: You provide such essential service to our entire neighborhood.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Serious">>
Raju: Surely there's some small way I could assist without causing problems?

<<SetCharacterExpression "MunnaBhai" "Quizzical">>
MunnaBhai: You really want to learn about mechanical work?

<<SetCharacterExpression "MunnaBhai" "Skeptical">>
MunnaBhai: Even knowing how demanding customers can be when their transportation fails?

<<SetCharacterExpression "MunnaBhai" "Worried">>
MunnaBhai: How precise tire repair must be? How exhausting these long days become?

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Confident">>
Raju: I'm not afraid of hard work or demanding customers, bhai.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Proud">>
Raju: My father always says that skilled trades are the foundation of any community.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Determined">>
Raju: I want to understand what that really means.

<<SetCharacterExpression "MunnaBhai" "Quizzical">>
MunnaBhai: Hmm. Most young people these days only want easy office jobs.

<<SetCharacterExpression "MunnaBhai" "Disappointed">>
MunnaBhai: But come back tomorrow morning if you're serious. We'll talk more then.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Overjoyed">>
Raju: Thank you, bhai! I'll be here early tomorrow!

<<HideCharacter>>
As Raju leaves the busy shop, the sounds of mechanical work and customer negotiations fill his ears. Munna Bhai's initial skepticism has only strengthened his determination to prove his genuine commitment to learning.

<<set $MunnaBhai_Day = 2>>
<<EndEvent true>>
===

title: MunnaBhai_Day2
tags: 
---

<<PlayBackgroundMusic Light_3>>
<<SetBGSprite MunnaTyreShop>>

// Scene Setup - Day 2 during morning setup period
True to his word, Raju returns during the peaceful morning setup period to observe how Munna Bhai prepares for the day's work.

The shop emanates methodical efficiency as Munna Bhai systematically checks tools and organizes repair materials. The peaceful atmosphere contrasts sharply with yesterday's chaos.

<<SetCharacterExpression "MunnaBhai" "Astonished">>
MunnaBhai: Back again, beta? I thought yesterday might have scared you off!

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Excited">>
Raju: Not at all, bhai! Actually, I couldn't stop thinking about your work.

<<SetCharacterExpression "MunnaBhai" "Quizzical">>
MunnaBhai: Oh? What were you thinking about?

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Excited">>
Raju: How you use such simple hand tools to diagnose problems and create precise repairs.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Smiling">>
Raju: I've never seen anything like it before!

<<SetCharacterExpression "MunnaBhai" "Disappointed">>
MunnaBhai: Fascinated by mechanical work? That's rare these days, beta.

<<SetCharacterExpression "MunnaBhai" "Sad">>
MunnaBhai: Society doesn't value mechanics the way they should.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Quizzical">>
Raju: What do you mean, bhai?

<<SetCharacterExpression "MunnaBhai" "Sad">>
MunnaBhai: People need our services desperately but don't respect our skills.

<<SetCharacterExpression "MunnaBhai" "Irritated">>
MunnaBhai: They want instant, cheap fixes instead of quality work that lasts.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Quizzical">>
Raju: How did you learn such detailed repair techniques?

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Excited">>
Raju: Did someone teach you?

<<SetCharacterExpression "MunnaBhai" "Smiling">>
MunnaBhai: My uncle was a bicycle mechanic. I started helping him at age ten.

<<SetCharacterExpression "MunnaBhai" "Proud">>
MunnaBhai: Eighteen years I've been perfecting these techniques.

<<SetCharacterExpression "MunnaBhai" "Serious">>
MunnaBhai: Learning to diagnose problems by sound, touch, and experience.

<<SetCharacterExpression "MunnaBhai" "Disappointed">>
MunnaBhai: But young people today want office jobs - they think mechanical work is beneath them.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Serious">>
Raju: That must be frustrating, bhai.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Sad">>
Raju: When people don't understand how much expertise this work requires.

<<SetCharacterExpression "MunnaBhai" "Irritated">>
MunnaBhai: They don't understand that every repair requires problem-solving and precision.

<<SetCharacterExpression "MunnaBhai" "Worried">>
MunnaBhai: When someone's transportation fails, their entire day is ruined.

<<SetCharacterExpression "MunnaBhai" "Proud">>
MunnaBhai: But when my repairs work perfectly? People can earn their living, children get to school, families function.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Excited">>
Raju: That's exactly why I want to learn, bhai!

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Determined">>
Raju: Mechanical skills create immediate, practical value for people's daily lives.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Serious">>
Raju: I don't want to miss the chance to understand such important knowledge.

<<SetCharacterExpression "MunnaBhai" "Quizzical">>
MunnaBhai: You keep expressing interest, but let me ask you something.

<<SetCharacterExpression "MunnaBhai" "Serious">>
MunnaBhai: Mechanical training means different levels of responsibility and skill.

<<SetCharacterExpression "MunnaBhai" "Skeptical">>
MunnaBhai: What exactly do you think you could contribute to professional bicycle repair?

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Confused">>
Raju: That's a good question, bhai. Let me think about it properly.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Determined">>
Raju: Can I come back tomorrow with a better answer?

<<SetCharacterExpression "MunnaBhai" "Smiling">>
MunnaBhai: Yes, beta. Think carefully about what you want to learn and how you can help.

<<HideCharacter>>
As their conversation concludes, Raju recognizes that Munna Bhai's question represents a shift from polite dismissal to serious consideration. The mechanic's frustration about society's undervaluation of skilled trades has transformed his motivation into genuine respect.

<<set $MunnaBhai_Day = 3>>
<<EndEvent true>>
